WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.567
The third graders were restless.

2
00:00:02.568 --> 00:00:07.494
They wanted to be playing outdoors, not sitting in the classroom.

3
00:00:07.495 --> 00:00:10.269
Mr. Higgins stood in front of the class.

4
00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:13.856
"What happens in spring?" he asked.

5
00:00:13.857 --> 00:00:18.622
"We plan for summer vacation!" said Katie.

6
00:00:18.623 --> 00:00:21.231
"True," said Mr. Higgins.

7
00:00:21.232 --> 00:00:23.546
"But it's not time for that yet, Katie.

8
00:00:23.547 --> 00:00:25.918
Who has another answer?"

9
00:00:25.919 --> 00:00:29.464
"Flowers bloom!" said Laura.

10
00:00:29.465 --> 00:00:33.387
"Birds build nests!" said Joy.

11
00:00:33.388 --> 00:00:38.069
"Good," said Mr. Higgins. "What about the weather?"

12
00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:44.460
"Sunny and warm," Katie said, looking out the window with longing.

13
00:00:44.461 --> 00:00:49.043
"But sometimes it can be stormy," said Luke.

14
00:00:49.044 --> 00:00:52.535
"Twisters!" said Carlos Ramirez.

15
00:00:52.536 --> 00:00:55.856
He lived two houses down from Luke.

16
00:00:55.857 --> 00:00:58.592
"That's right," said Mr. Higgins.

17
00:00:58.593 --> 00:01:02.547
"Twisters, or tornadoes, often strike in the spring.

18
00:01:02.548 --> 00:01:06.228
Who can explain what a tornado is?"

19
00:01:06.229 --> 00:01:08.241
Carlos spoke up again.

20
00:01:08.242 --> 00:01:12.035
"It's a strong wind that spins around and around.

21
00:01:12.036 --> 00:01:17.329
It's shaped like a funnel, and it hangs down from a storm cloud.

22
00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:20.779
A tornado can carry off a cow or a school bus.

23
00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:24.491
It can even lift a house up in the air!"

24
00:01:24.492 --> 00:01:29.536
"Tornadoes are very dangerous," agreed Mr. Higgins.

25
00:01:29.537 --> 00:01:32.240
"That's why every spring we prepare.

26
00:01:32.241 --> 00:01:36.016
We practice what to do if a tornado comes."

27
00:01:36.017 --> 00:01:40.780
"Are we going to have a tornado drill?" Katie asked hopefully.

28
00:01:40.781 --> 00:01:44.283
"Yes, Katie. Later," said Mr. Higgins.

29
00:01:44.284 --> 00:01:48.811
"Now who remembers what the tornado alarm sounds like?"

30
00:01:48.812 --> 00:01:53.327
"Three siren blasts!" said Luke.

31
00:01:53.328 --> 00:01:56.057
"Yes," said Mr. Higgins.

32
00:01:56.058 --> 00:02:00.612
"Then we all get in line, and I lead the way to the basement."

33
00:02:00.613 --> 00:02:04.736
"And when we get there, we take cover!" said Katie.

34
00:02:04.737 --> 00:02:08.506
"HA! That's the best part!"

35
00:02:08.507 --> 00:02:11.589
"Thank you, Katie," said Mr. Higgins.

36
00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:15.783
"Now who wants to demonstrate the take-cover position?"

37
00:02:15.784 --> 00:02:19.010
"I do!" cried Katie.

38
00:02:19.011 --> 00:02:23.637
"Please settle down, Katie," said Mr. Higgins, frowning a little.

39
00:02:23.638 --> 00:02:27.186
"Carlos, why don't you show us?"

40
00:02:27.187 --> 00:02:29.751
Carlos walked to the front of the class.

41
00:02:29.752 --> 00:02:34.666
He knelt on the floor and put his arms and hands over his head. "Perfect!"

42
00:02:34.667 --> 00:02:37.912
said Mr. Higgins. The

43
00:02:37.913 --> 00:02:40.087
third graders cheered. Carlos

44
00:02:40.088 --> 00:02:44.025
grinned and returned to his desk. "We're

45
00:02:44.026 --> 00:02:47.484
ready for the drill!" said Mr. Higgins. "Now

46
00:02:47.485 --> 00:02:50.141
get out your math homework." Everybody

47
00:02:50.142 --> 00:02:52.860
groaned. After

48
00:02:52.861 --> 00:02:56.610
math came social studies and then lunch. When

49
00:02:56.611 --> 00:03:02.113
the children returned from the lunchroom, it was time for art. "Let's

50
00:03:02.114 --> 00:03:06.183
work on our tornado posters," announced Mr. Higgins. "Katie,

51
00:03:06.184 --> 00:03:09.780
please pass out the magic markers." Katie

52
00:03:09.781 --> 00:03:17.927
grabbed the coffee can filled with markers when suddenly— weeee-uuuuu, weeee-uuuuu, weeee-uuuuu .

53
00:03:17.928 --> 00:03:22.389
Katie jumped and the markers flew into the air.

54
00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:26.142
"Tornado drill!" shouted Luke.

55
00:03:26.143 --> 00:03:29.720
The speaker on the wall crackled and hissed.

56
00:03:29.721 --> 00:03:33.332
Then Ms. Olson's voice filled the room.

57
00:03:33.333 --> 00:03:36.302
"Students!" the principal reminded them.

58
00:03:36.303 --> 00:03:39.261
"Go immediately to the basement."

59
00:03:39.262 --> 00:03:42.431
Everyone moved toward the door except Katie.

60
00:03:42.432 --> 00:03:45.056
She was picking up markers.

61
00:03:45.057 --> 00:03:48.503
"Get in line, Katie," Joy said.

62
00:03:48.504 --> 00:03:51.388
"I am," Katie snapped back.

63
00:03:51.389 --> 00:03:55.507
She hated it when Joy told her what to do.

64
00:03:55.508 --> 00:03:58.263
The third graders followed Mr. Higgins.

65
00:03:58.264 --> 00:04:01.415
They went down the stairs to the basement.

66
00:04:01.416 --> 00:04:06.215
Other students entered the basement from all directions.

67
00:04:06.216 --> 00:04:12.355
"Everybody down!" Mr. Higgins called as soon as everyone was standing by the wall.

68
00:04:12.356 --> 00:04:16.983
All the children dropped to the floor in the take-cover position.

69
00:04:16.984 --> 00:04:20.739
Ms. Olson held up her stopwatch and gave it a click.

70
00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:26.018
"Two minutes exactly," she said. "Good work, everyone!"

71
00:04:26.019 --> 00:04:31.371
Back in the classroom, Mr. Higgins passed out a paper to each student.

72
00:04:31.372 --> 00:04:34.254
"We'll finish our posters later.

73
00:04:34.255 --> 00:04:40.408
This is a list of things you can do at home to get ready for tornado season," he said.

74
00:04:40.409 --> 00:04:45.029
"You should each organize a Family Tornado Safety Team."

75
00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:48.391
"Cool," said Luke.

76
00:04:48.392 --> 00:04:53.336
"The Ramirez Tornado Safety Team!" said Carlos.

77
00:04:53.337 --> 00:04:58.379
"The Donovan Tornado Safety Team!" said Katie.

78
00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:03.568
She scribbled something on a piece of notebook paper and then passed it to Joy.

79
00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:12.462
Joy frowned. She could already guess what her sister's note said: I'll be captain!

